--[[
================================================================================

        H E L L I S H   T I M E   E V E R

            _G.Time   = 0      -- optional: seconds before it starts
            _G.Random = true   -- optional: false = entities only come with K
            loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bonellocristian78-lab/Gradish-Mode/main/HellishTimeEver"))()

            K   an entity, now. Spam it: every press is one more.

        Run it inside a DOORS run. Everything on screen is DOORS' own, cloned
        from DOORS while you play: its fonts, its red flash, its jumpscare
        text, its vignette, its modifier panel, its sounds, its camera shake.
        Nothing is drawn or played from outside the game.

        THE TWO SETTINGS
        ----------------
        _G.Time    Seconds after the loadstring before Hellish Time Ever
                   starts. Missing or 0: it starts at once.
        _G.Random  true, the default: entities also come on their own, one
                   every AUTO_MIN to AUTO_MAX seconds, at random -- and K
                   still works on top. false: they only come when you press K.

        HOW IT STARTS
        -------------
        The screen goes black. DOORS' red flash hits with Dread's boom and
        the camera shakes; HELLISH TIME EVER comes up in the font of DOORS'
        "YOU ARE DEAD" jumpscare text, in moving black and white, with
        DOORS' knob badge under it: +666%. Then back to the game, and DOORS'
        modifier panel slides in with Hellish Time Ever on top and +666% on
        the knob bonus.

        EVERY ENTITY
        ------------
        A red flash, a kick of the camera, the sound DOORS makes when a
        modifier is added, the lights of your room red for a moment, and the
        counter at the top -- DOORS' own "MODIFIERS ACTIVATED" label -- goes
        up: HELLISH x7   SPEED 150.

        THE HELL RISES
        --------------
        Every entity turns the rooms a little redder and darker, muffles the
        sound a little more -- an equalizer in SoundService.Main, the same
        group DOORS puts its own Sanity and Oxygen equalizers in -- and turns
        Dread's ambience up. After HEAT_FULL entities it is as far as it goes.

        NEVER THE SAME ONE TWICE
        ------------------------
        A bag, not dice: every entity is in it once and each one pulls one
        out. When it is empty it fills up again by itself, and the first of
        the new round is never the last of the old one. Speed keeps climbing
        from BASE_SPEED to MAX_SPEED, where 100 is Rush's normal pace.

        SPAM
        ----
        Every model and script is downloaded once, at the start, so a press
        spawns at once instead of waiting for a download. One that could not
        be loaded is skipped and the next one comes instead.

        NOTHING GIVEN AWAY
        ------------------
        When it starts it switches off this repo's crucifix givers --
        CrucifixGiver, which would also answer every K, CorrodedCrucifixGiver
        and CrucifixAll -- and while it runs no badge of the mod is awarded.
        Honcho V2 comes without his crucifix and without his badges.

        WHERE THE ENTITIES COME FROM
        ----------------------------
            Rush, Ambush     Vynixu's own models, from the Entity Spawner repo
            A-60, A-120,     your models from Roblox Studio, exported to the
            Scribble, Bash,  HTE/ folder of this repo with their sounds
            Blitz
            Honcho V2        HonchoV2.lua from this repo -- without his
                             crucifix and without badges
            J-518            J-518 from this repo

        THE MODIFIER PANEL
        ------------------
        Built from DOORS' own panel, not an imitation of it. When a run starts
        with modifiers, DOORS clones MainUI.Modifiers, adds one row per
        modifier, writes "N MODIFIERS ACTIVATED" and takes it away after ten
        seconds. This does the same thing, with the same pieces.

        It does NOT add Hellish Time Ever to DOORS' modifier list itself.
        DOORS reads every active modifier's knob bonus from its own table, and
        a name that is not in that table would crash DOORS' own script. The
        +666% is written on the panel only.

================================================================================
]]

